Value destination (.*)
Value gateway (.*)
Value vlan (.*)
Value type (.*)
Value sub_type (.*)
Value metric (.*)
Value distance (.*)

# Parse the output of "show ip route" on an HP AOS-S switch.
#
# Fixed-column table (term width 200 at collection time), 1-based column
# starts: Destination 3, Gateway 22, VLAN 38, Type 43, Sub-Type 53,
# Metric 64, Dist 75. Gateway and VLAN are blank on some rows, so after
# anchoring on the CIDR in the Destination column the remaining fields are
# matched positionally with fixed-width slices; parse.go trims the trailing
# spaces out of each captured field (a blank field becomes ""). The CIDR
# anchor also keeps the column header and the separator line from matching.


Start
  ^  (?P<destination>\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+/\d{1,2}) +(?P<gateway>.{16})(?P<vlan>.{5})(?P<type>.{10})(?P<sub_type>.{11})(?P<metric>.{11})(?P<distance>\S+)\s*$ -> Record
